# Identity

Fix commit: `f6fc7ac656629a39e0508726b505f861c5524a96`.
Published version: `0.2.51-nightly.20261020-193048.f6fc7ac`.
Nightly CI: 39483409734 passed. Publish to npm: 39483409740 passed.
Registry nightly gitHead and version matched the exact fix commit.
Published tarball SHA-256: `ea0b0e9c1c7ed9003f3f9d25abd9f63efeee6b86deb4a1283b9c81f1def251ef`.
Published tarball had 485 files and no journal payload was used for installation.

# Local deployment

The exact published tarball was acquired with SHA-1/SHA-512 verification and
extracted into the task evidence directory. npm global installation from the
verified tarball succeeded. A new non-overwriting snapshot was installed at
`%USERPROFILE%\.local\share\ciel-runtime-f6fc7ac656629a39e0508726b505f861c5524a96`.
User `CIEL_RUNTIME_HOME` now points to that snapshot. The direct registry
version install was attempted first but failed with ETARGET while the publish
verification endpoint was still propagating; the verified local tarball path
was then used, with no weakened verification.

# Verification

- Installed focused suites: 375 run, zero failures/errors, 80 skipped.
- Recursive source integrity: 430 Python files checked for snapshot and npm
  global package; zero mismatches against the verified tarball.
- Snapshot version command: exit 0,
  `ciel-runtime 0.2.51-nightly.20261020-193048.f6fc7ac`.
- Native installed acceptance `run-codex-remote-installed-f6fc7ac-144153` passed:
  same-thread restart, Leave paused dismissal, unchanged paused goal, new external
  input replied, old native process gone, app-server port release observed.
  Both owned listeners were absent after teardown.
- Screenshot attempt could not capture a window; rendered terminal text shows
  `STUB-REPLY-9` and `Goal paused (/goal resume)`. Initial AttachConsole error 6
  is preserved in the owned harness record; subsequent captures and acceptance
  succeeded.

# Live-session safety

No live Bob, Walkie, or local runtime session was restarted. Pre-install process
identities were captured in `evidence/preinstall.json`; installation used a new
full-SHA snapshot and did not overwrite the prior `9ac82f0` snapshot. Existing
processes therefore remain on their previously loaded code.
